    "body": "Bumps [fast-uri](https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri) from 3.1.8 to 3.1.9.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases\">fast-uri's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v3.1.9</h2>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<p>This security release fixes four URI parsing and normalization vulnerabilities in fast-uri 3.x. Applications that process untrusted URI input should upgrade to v3.1.9.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Medium \u2014 URI scheme spoofing through percent-encoded schemes</strong> (<a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-w74x-v6f9-j3xg\">GHSA-w74x-v6f9-j3xg</a>, CVE-2026-110306): percent-encoded scheme input is now rejected instead of being decoded into a live scheme.</li>\n<li><strong>Medium \u2014 Host confusion during domain-host canonicalization</strong> (<a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-wjr9-j795-jxcr\">GHSA-wjr9-j795-jxcr</a>, CVE-2026-110180): malformed domain hosts containing ambiguous delimiters or stripped control characters are now rejected instead of being silently rewritten.</li>\n<li><strong>Low \u2014 Incorrect relative-reference normalization</strong> (<a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-xhq7-xmqj-769h\">GHSA-xhq7-xmqj-769h</a>, CVE-2026-110095): dot-segment removal now preserves the resolution semantics of relative references.</li>\n<li><strong>Low \u2014 Scheme injection in suffix references</strong> (<a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp\">GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp</a>, CVE-2026-110725): first-segment colons in path-only suffix references are now escaped so the output is not reparsed as a scheme.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Upgrade with:</p>\n<pre lang=\"sh\"><code>npm install fast-uri@3.1.9\n</code></pre>\n<p>Thanks to <a href=\"https://github.com/zekth\"><code>@\u200bzekth</code></a> for reporting the scheme, host, and relative-reference issues, and to <a href=\"https://github.com/UlisesGascon\"><code>@\u200bUlisesGascon</code></a> for finding the suffix-reference issue and reviewing the remediations.</p>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>ci: enable trusted publishing releases (v3.x) by <a href=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@\u200bmcollina</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastify/fast-uri/pull/229\">fastify/fast-uri#229</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/compare/v3.1.8...v3.1.9\">https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/compare/v3.1.8...v3.1.9</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/0def70338a0fa2f12a10c83ae8eafc2139ae9a07\"><code>0def703</code></a> Bumped v3.1.9</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/a1d0da2f5c703244027c1b204c1aebd0516da338\"><code>a1d0da2</code></a> test: generate only relative path references</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/9eb8759a9825c046f57f7f695f1944bc39b88abd\"><code>9eb8759</code></a> fix: preserve relative paths in suffix and relative resolution</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/54c30f75891b74e5a4393b44be9ea7ba43dd1e4b\"><code>54c30f7</code></a> docs: note suffix-reference authority ambiguity</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/39e6493c1356f30a0084171627eb266786e1620e\"><code>39e6493</code></a> fix: escape a first-segment colon in suffix references</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/745183c1d9d98d113bed8a57bb1c9ceaf0147b7a\"><code>745183c</code></a> test: cover first-segment colon in suffix references</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/ddfc6a51122dfce0365655f04479fc3adb7f6b3c\"><code>ddfc6a5</code></a> fix(SEC-03): reject non reg-name characters in domain hosts</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/d86a8d29f45187819dac2d4fe171c35e3e488264\"><code>d86a8d2</code></a> fix: keep a colon-first segment behind &quot;./&quot; in relative normalization</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/eb483b5da2580bdecb8af644bbfee878d5424850\"><code>eb483b5</code></a> test: cover colon-first relative references in normalization</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/b110a3571c37dfcf9d1c72ce2e2e178c78d1a424\"><code>b110a35</code></a> fix(SEC-02): preserve meaning of relative references during normalization</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/compare/v3.1.8...v3.1.9\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Maintainer changes</summary>\n<p>This version was pushed to npm by <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/~GitHub%20Actions\">GitHub Actions</a>, a new releaser for fast-uri since your current version.</p>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=fast-uri&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=3.1.8&new-version=3.1.9)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the [Security Alerts page](https://github.com/mateu/graphrag-notes/network/alerts).\n\n</details>",
